WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.202
Let’s run our first complete example with variables.

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:11.777
Sales is one thousand, costs is eight hundred, and profit is calculated by subtracting costs from sales.

00:00:11.777 --> 00:00:17.377
So before you run the cell, you should already expect profit to be two hundred.

00:00:17.377 --> 00:00:21.944
The print statements simply make those three values visible in the output.

00:00:22.713 --> 00:00:28.465
Now change sales from one thousand to twelve hundred fifty and run the cell again.

00:00:28.465 --> 00:00:32.445
Notice that you do not need to rewrite the profit formula.

00:00:32.445 --> 00:00:36.835
Python automatically uses the new value of sales.

00:00:36.835 --> 00:00:44.658
That is a basic but important idea in analytics: the logic can stay the same even when the data changes.
